    "note": "Original coarse symmetric geometry; no Cadw drawing was traced. The square clear court is sqrt(3000) m across, then 4.7 m inner curtains and an approximate 18 m separation of outer faces give an outer curtain about 100 m across before tower projections. This is not the plan’s rough 90 m estimate. Octagonal outer circuit, tower radii 3.5/5 m, gatehouses 16 × 8 m and outer height 6 m are approximate. Inner curtain is 11 m and inner towers stop at 13 m (+2 m); inner gates stop at 11 m, without completed upper storeys. Doors, floor divisions and stairs are schematic. Flat open caps preserve both courts."
